+<p>The native implementation carries whole IPv4 packets over TLS; it does
+not implement a userspace TCP stack. Six loopback TLS integration tests
+cover authentication, rejected credentials, certificate trust and channel
+identity binding, IPv4 TCP/UDP/ICMP echo and malformed framing. These are
+mock tests, not evidence of all those protocols on a real gateway. Live
+native probes received TCP SYN-ACK and ICMP port-unreachable in response to
+UDP; ICMP echo did not receive a reply. System TUN/routing validation remains
+separate from raw packet probes.</p>
+
+<p>Session tokens are bound to a live authenticated control channel. A
+separate <tt>--authenticate</tt> invocation followed by cookie-only startup
+is unsupported. Channel failure requires fresh authentication; no seamless
+session resumption is claimed. HTTP proxying, IPv6 and DTLS are unsupported.</p>
+
+<p>A two-hour idle SSH test of the separate minimal TCP forwarder failed to
+resume application traffic although VPN heartbeats continued. Native and
+prototype long-term stability must not be inferred from heartbeat replies.
+Other authentication methods, firmware versions, compression, session
+renewal, disconnect messages and multi-hour stability remain unverified.
+Further redacted observations and
 an implementation following the existing
 <a href="mitm.html">protocol investigation guidance</a> are welcome.</p>
 
